      "18409": {
        "comments": [
          {
            "creator": "Andre.Gillibert",
            "is_markdown": true,
            "attachment_id": 3068,
            "time": "2022-09-25T19:09:35Z",
            "creation_time": "2022-09-25T19:09:35Z",
            "text": "Created attachment 3068\npatch fixing the issue\n\n# steps to reproduce\ndata.frame(x=42)[,\"y\"]\n# observe behavior\nError in `[.data.frame`(data.frame(x = 42), , \"y\") : \n  undefined columns selected\n# expected behavior\nError in `[.data.frame`(data.frame(x = 42), , \"y\") : \n  undefined column selected: `y'\n# solution\nThe attached patch to the R SVN trunk (2022-09-25) provides more descriptive error messages.\nIt specifies which columns are missing, for character or integer column indices. For logical vectors, it specifies whether a logical value is found out of bounds or if a NA value is found.\nIt also adds a French translation to the new messages.\n# can it break code?\nThis patch is designed not to change the behavior of `[.data.frame` but might break code that would rely on the character strings of error messages, such as code using try() to catch an error, then grepl() or `==` to interpret the error message. That could would already broken when non-english translations of error messages are used.",
            "bug_id": 18409,
            "count": 0,
            "tags": [],
            "id": 99063,
            "is_private": false
          },
          {
            "time": "2022-09-25T19:10:49Z",
            "id": 99064,
            "is_private": false,
            "tags": [],
            "attachment_id": 3069,
            "text": "Created attachment 3069\ntest script",
            "bug_id": 18409,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 1,
            "creator": "Andre.Gillibert",
            "creation_time": "2022-09-25T19:10:49Z"
          },
          {
            "attachment_id": 3070,
            "tags": [],
            "id": 99065,
            "time": "2022-09-26T07:38:28Z",
            "is_private": false,
            "creation_time": "2022-09-26T07:38:28Z",
            "creator": "Andre.Gillibert",
            "bug_id": 18409,
            "text": "Created attachment 3070\nupdated patch fixing the issue\n\nDucan Murdoch comments taken in account.\n1) Truncation of a short list of items with '...'\n2) Specification of the number of missing indices\nMoreover, for numeric/logical indices, the total number of columns of the data frame is specified",
            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 2
          },
          {
            "time": "2022-09-26T07:43:54Z",
            "attachment_id": 3071,
