            "text": "Created attachment 3071\nupdated test script\n\nUpdated test script for updated patch, testing the new code paths.",
            "creation_time": "2022-09-26T07:43:54Z"
          },
          {
            "attachment_id": {},
            "time": "2026-06-26T19:00:12Z",
            "creator": "zkamvar",
            "is_markdown": true,
            "tags": [],
            "is_private": false,
            "id": 103245,
            "creation_time": "2026-06-26T19:00:12Z",
            "count": 4,
            "text": "Hello from R dev day Cascadia R! We are reviewing this patch, but there are conflicts with the current R devel version: \n\n```\nC         b/src/library/base/R/dataframe.R\n>         rejected hunk @@ -597,6 +597,78 @@\n>         rejected hunk @@ -620,13 +692,13 @@\n>         rejected hunk @@ -646,12 +718,12 @@\n>         rejected hunk @@ -694,7 +766,7 @@\nC         b/src/library/base/po/R-base.pot\n>         rejected hunk @@ -1,8 +1,8 @@\n>         rejected hunk @@ -282,13 +282,16 @@\n>         rejected hunk @@ -1699,6 +1702,16 @@\nC         b/src/library/base/po/R-fr.po\n>         rejected hunk @@ -5,11 +5,11 @@\n>         rejected hunk @@ -308,15 +308,18 @@\n>         rejected hunk @@ -1926,6 +1929,16 @@\nC         b/src/library/base/man/base-internal.Rd\n>         rejected hunk @@ -15,6 +15,7 @@\n>         rejected hunk @@ -82,6 +83,8 @@\n>         rejected hunk @@ -206,6 +209,9 @@\nSummary of conflicts:\n  Text conflicts: 4\n```\n\nWe re-applied the original changes in dataframe.R and are going to upload a patch. \n\nWe confirmed that this patch works as expected.",
            "bug_id": 18409
          },
          {
            "time": "2026-06-26T20:27:08Z",
            "id": 103247,
            "is_private": false,
            "attachment_id": 3740,
            "tags": [],
            "text": "Created attachment 3740\nupdated error message; removed non-R changes\n\nWe applied the function from the previous patch to the most current revision (90194), but we have removed the po, pot, and Rd files. We also updated the language of the error message because no plural is needed for counting multiple columns.",
            "bug_id": 18409,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 5,
            "creator": "zkamvar",
            "creation_time": "2026-06-26T20:27:08Z"
          },
          {
            "time": "2026-11-13T23:42:53Z",
            "id": 104227,
            "is_private": false,
            "attachment_id": {},
            "tags": [],
            "text": "Overall I like this feature, though I haven't done a technical deep dive on the updated patch yet. One small tweak that I'd propose is the message should say something along the lines of, `sprintf(\"%d undefined columns selected; first %d: %s\", <unmatched>, min(<unmatched>, maxlen), <pasted undefined cols>)`, and similarly for the indices case, ie indicating whether the displayed list of undefined columns was truncated or not.\n\nIs this something you would want to work on @Zhian (and/or other CascadiaR folks) or would you prefer i pick it up from here?",
            "bug_id": 18409,
            "count": 6,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "creator": "gabembecker",
            "creation_time": "2026-11-13T23:42:53Z"
          }
        ]
      }
